c.UG,{remarkPlugins:[l.Z],className:"prose-base max-w-4xl md:prose-lg prose-a:text-sky-400",children:'\n**Last updated:** October 28, 2026\n\n## 1. **Introduction**\n\nWelcome to Upscayl (“Company”, “we”, “our”, “us”). We provide an online AI Image upscaling and enhancement platform. These Terms and Conditions ("Terms") govern your use of our website, services, and software (collectively referred to as the "Service"). By accessing or using the Service, you agree to be bound by these Terms. \n\nSupplemental terms and conditions or documents that may be posted on the Services from time to time are hereby expressly incorporated herein by reference. We reserve the right, in our sole discretion, to make changes or modifications to these Legal Terms from time to time. We will alert you about any changes by updating the "Last updated" date of these Legal Terms, and you waive any right to receive specific notice of each such change. It is your responsibility to periodically review these Legal Terms to stay informed of updates. You will be subject to, and will be deemed to have been made aware of and to have accepted, the changes in any revised Legal Terms by your continued use of the Services after the date such revised Legal Terms are posted.\n\nThe Services are intended for users who are at least 13 years of age. All users who are minors in the jurisdiction in which they reside (generally under the age of 18) must have the permission of, and be directly supervised by, their parent or guardian to use the Services. If you are a minor, you must have your parent or guardian read and agree to these Legal Terms prior to you using the Services. If you do not agree with any part of these Terms, please refrain from using our Service.\n\n## 2. **Eligibility**\n\nTo use our Service, you must:\n- Be at least 13 years old.\n- Have the legal capacity to enter into binding contracts.\n- Not have previously been banned from using our Service.\n\nBy using our Service, you represent and warrant that you meet these eligibility requirements.\n\n## 3. **Accounts**\n\nTo access certain features of our Service, you must create an account. When you create an account, you must provide accurate and complete information. You are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of your account credentials and for all activities that occur under your account. You must notify us immediately of any unauthorized use of your account.\n\nWe reserve the right to terminate your account at our discretion if we find any breach of these Terms.\n\n## 4. **Subscription Plans and Payments**\n\nOur Service operates on a subscription-based model. By subscribing, you agree to pay the applicable subscription fees as indicated at the time of subscription. All payments are processed by our payment provider, Dodo Payments, which acts as our Merchant of Record and is subject to its own terms and conditions. Subscriptions that were started earlier through Lemon Squeezy or PayPal continue to be processed by those providers until they end. \n\n### **Billing and Renewal**\n- Your subscription will automatically renew at the end of each billing cycle unless you cancel it through your account settings.\n- If you cancel, your subscription stays active until the end of the billing period you have already paid for, and it will not renew after that.\n- If a renewal payment fails, your subscription may be placed on hold. While it is on hold, you cannot use your subscription credits until you update your payment method. Credits you bought as one-time purchases remain available.\n- Subscription fees are non-refundable unless otherwise stated in our refund policy.\n\n## 5. **Use of the Service**\n\n### **Permitted Use**\nYou agree to use the Service solely for lawful purposes and in accordance with these Terms. You are prohibited from:\n- Using the Service in any way that violates any applicable local, national, or international law.\n- Uploading any content that infringes intellectual property rights, is harmful, offensive, or otherwise violates our content policies, including the Prohibited Content rules in Section 6.\n- Engaging in any unauthorized scraping, data mining, or similar data gathering activities.\n\n### **File Upload and Processing**\nWhen you upload a file to our platform, you retain full ownership of your content. We only use, store, modify, and distribute your content as necessary to provide the Service to you with your consent.\n\nYour images will not be used to train any AI models.\n\nYour data is encrypted and stored securely on our servers according to the encryption standards provided by AWS and Google Firebase. We are committed to safeguarding your data and employ industry-standard measures to ensure secure file processing. While we strive to provide a seamless experience, we cannot guarantee that uploads and processing will always be error-free or uninterrupted.\n\n\n## 6. **Prohibited Content and Moderation**\n\nAdult, sexually explicit, and NSFW content is not allowed on Upscayl Cloud. This applies to images you upload or edit and to prompts you write for our AI image generation features.\n\nWe moderate the Service to keep it that way. Images and prompts may be screened by automated systems and reviewed by our team. We may block a request, remove content, or suspend or terminate an account that breaks this rule, as described in Section 11 (Termination).\n\nIf you see something that shouldn\'t be here, please let us know at [support@upscayl.org](mailto:support@upscayl.org).\n\n## 7. **Intellectual Property**\n\nThe Service and all associated content, including but not limited to software, design, logos, and trademarks, are owned by or licensed to the Company and are protected by applicable copyright, trademark, and other intellectual property laws.\n\nYou may not reproduce, distribute, or create derivative works from any part of the Service without express written permission from the Company.\n\n## 8. **Third-Party Services**\n\nOur Service may integrate with third-party services, including our payment provider, Dodo Payments. By using these third-party services, you agree to their respective terms of use and privacy policies. We are not responsible for the performance or reliability of these third-party services.\n\n## 9. **Limitation of Liability**\n\nTo the fullest extent permitted by law, the Company and its affiliates, directors, employees, and agents shall not be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages arising from your use of the Service or inability to access the Service, including but not limited to errors, interruptions, or delays in file processing.\n\nOur total liability to you for any claims arising out of or related to your use of the Service shall not exceed the total amount paid by you to us in the twelve months preceding the claim.\n\n## 10. **Disclaimer of Warranties**\n\nThe Service is provided "as is" and "as available" without warranties of any kind, whether express or implied, including but not limited to the implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement.\n\nWe do not warrant that the Service will meet your specific requirements, operate uninterrupted, be free of errors, or that any defects will be corrected.\n\n## 11. **Termination**\n\nWe may suspend or terminate your account or access to the Service at any time, for any reason, including but not limited to a breach of these Terms. Upon termination, you will no longer have access to the Service, and any content associated with your account may be deleted.\n\n## 12. **Changes to the Terms**\n\nWe reserve the right to update or modify these Terms at any time. Any changes will be posted on this page, and the “Last Updated” date at the top will reflect the most recent version. Your continued use of the Service after any changes constitutes your acceptance of the revised Terms.\n\n## 13. **Governing Law and Dispute Resolution**\n\nThese Terms are governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of India. Any dispute arising out of or in connection with these Legal Terms, including any question regarding its existence, validity, or termination, shall be referred to and finally resolved by the International Commercial Arbitration Court under the European Arbitration Chamber (Belgium, Brussels, Avenue Louise, 146) according to the Rules of this ICAC, which, as a result of referring to it, is considered as the part of this clause. The number of arbitrators shall be three (3). The seat, or legal place, or arbitration shall be New Delhi, India. The language of the proceedings shall be English. The governing law of these Legal Terms shall be substantive law of India.\n\n## 14. **Contact Information**\n\nIf you have any questions or concerns about these Terms, you may contact us at:\n\n**Email:** [support@upscayl.org](mailto:support@upscayl.org)  \n\n## 15. **Refund Policy**\n\nWe want you to be satisfied with Upscayl Cloud. This section explains when refunds may be issued and how long they take.\n\n### **Eligibility for Refunds**\n\nYou may be eligible for a refund if any of the following conditions apply:\n\n- You were charged in error (duplicate charge or incorrect amount)\n- You experienced a verified technical issue that prevented successful use of purchased credits\n\nRefunds are not offered for:\n\n- Unused credits after you cancel or renew your subscription\n- Dissatisfaction with model output quality when the service functioned as intended\n- Promotional or free credits\n\n### **Processing Time**\n\n- We typically review refund requests within 3–5 business days of receiving your request at support@upscayl.org.\n- If approved, we initiate the refund immediately after approval.\n\n### **Funds Return Timeline**\n\n- Once a refund is processed, our payment processor estimates it takes 5–10 business days for funds to return to the original payment method.\n- Your bank or card issuer may take additional time to post the funds.\n\n### **How to Request a Refund**\n\nPlease email us at [support@upscayl.org](mailto:support@upscayl.org) from your account email with:\n\n- Your account email and payment receipt/transaction ID\n- Date of charge and amount\n- Reason for the refund request\n'})]})}),(0,r.jsx)(s.Z,{}),(0,r.jsx)(a.Z,{})]})},68130:function(e,t,n){"use strict";n.d(t,{eW:function(){return r},hn:function(){return o}});let r=195e3,o={PUBLIC_ACCESS:!0,MAX_FILE_SIZE:52428800,MAX_FILES_LENGTH:20,WEBP_MAX_RESOLUTION:16383,JPEG_MAX_RESOLUTION:65535,MAX_TRIAL_INPUT_RESOLUTION:8,MAX_BASIC_INPUT_RESOLUTION:64,MAX_BUSINESS_INPUT_RESOLUTION:64,MAX_TRIAL_OUTPUT_RESOLUTION:16,MAX_BASIC_OUTPUT_RESOLUTION:256,MAX_BUSINESS_OUTPUT_RESOLUTION:512}},89302:function(e,t,n){"use strict";n.d(t,{Q:function(){return r}});let r={NOT_STARTED:"NOT_STARTED",SELECTED_FILE:"SELECTED_FILE",UPLOADING:"UPLOADING",UPLOAD_FAILED:"UPLOAD_FAILED",UPLOADED:"UPLOADED",UPSCALING:"UPSCALING",ENHANCING:"ENHANCING",PROCESSING:"PROCESSING",PROCESSED:"PROCESSED",PROCESS_FAILED:"PROCESS_FAILED"}}},function(e){e.O(0,[9102,3467,1154,5123,2598,419,2230,2888,9774,179],function(){return e(e.s=84523)}),_N_E=e.O()}]);